    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="1466" n="1444" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg1444"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357AB/12–2250: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the United
                        Kingdom </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d814-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-12-27T14:00:00-05:00">December 27,
                            1950—2 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3168. Brit Emb informed Dept Dec 26 favorable Cabinet decision to approach
                    GOI–GOP for informal talks Kashmir, other Indo-Pak differences during London
                    PriMin mtg. UK HICOMMs have recd instrs approach respective govts. We will treat
                    utmost confidence this subj (urtel 3573, Dec 22).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d814-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>We have noted (urtel 3558, Dec 20) UK appraisal of situation in Pak to effect
                    such is “not in any sense at point of crisis”. Although we sincerely hope this
                    is the case, our own analysis of situation is not reassuring. We believe there
                    are unmistakable signs growing unrest and mounting pressures against Liaquat
                    Govt and that opposition groups are using effectively Kashmir issue to weaken
                    Govt.</p>
                <pb facs="1467" n="1445" xml:id="pg1445"/>
                <p>We believe view tense world situation grave responsibility and challenge falls on
                    Indo-Pak leaders to settle their outstanding differences and hope Commonwealth
                    mtg with UK in mediatory role will provide means by which progress on Kashmir
                    and other Indo-Pak issues may be achieved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d814-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d814-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Karachi 349, New Delhi 983, USUN 611.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d814-f2" n="2" xml:id="d814-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 3573 from London, not printed, requested that the U.K. proposal for
                    discussing the Kashmir issue at the Commonwealth Prime Ministers meeting in
                    January be treated in utmost confidence (357.AB/12–2250).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
